+**B03-R1-01 — initialization metadata exceeds the configured byte quota: ADDRESSED.** `source/packages/lab-runtime/src/v2/simulation3d/physics-evidence.ts:61–67` now routes the initial manifest through `publish()`, which checks all existing stored bytes plus the complete new temporary-file byte cost before calling the atomic writer. `Buffer.byteLength` accounts for UTF-8 and escaped JSON. A healthy write also reserves a worst-case terminal manifest containing one gap, its reason and the intent bytes. Thus the previously demonstrated 1-byte budget cannot publish a 750-byte manifest or return a healthy recorder.
+
+**Check — related publication paths remain bounded.** The same guard covers reopen and terminal saves. The flush preflight at `physics-evidence.ts:73–77` includes the proposed chunk, intent, new manifest and terminal reserve while existing files remain counted. The actual publications are individually guarded as well. Append reserves terminal space before growing the WAL. The code does not spend above the budget to force a terminal write; a refused terminal save remains incomplete in memory/checkpoint. Conservative accounting of old targets or stale temporary files can refuse earlier but cannot increase the allowed bytes.
+
+**Check — focused regression coverage matches the finding.** `source/tests/integration/physics-evidence.test.ts:53–77` adds impossible initialization budgets, equal-character-count ASCII/Unicode metadata, worst-case escaped terminal/gap text, reopen with no temporary-file headroom, repeated terminal writes, and append failure with a persisted terminal/gap inside the configured cap. The initialization test requires zero stored bytes after refusal. These tests cover the original defect and the new reserve/publication logic rather than merely restating helper implementation.
+
+**Check — startup failure behavior remains explicit.** `source/tests/integration/mujoco-mobile-lifecycle.test.ts:119` adds an actual create followed by impossible physics initialization quota. It requires logical tick zero, `needs_attention`, an empty physics directory, `STARTUP_UNKNOWN` before and after reopen, and exactly one spawn. The fix changes the test helper only to pass this quota; it does not alter runner, Python, profile, schema or metric behavior.
