+- Durable, byte-bound trajectory chunks supply the goal and corridor observations; lossy UI telemetry is not the authority. The existing independent navigation geometry oracle recomputes path length, clearance and physical-contact constraint from raw drive poses instead of trusting report summary values. Per-engine path/clearance differences alone do not fail a study. IR-SIM contact/slip/tipping are explicitly unsupported with no zero-valued dynamics result.
+- Arrival measurement is the drive-frame pose at each Source `MissionArrived`. The registered policy is unchanged: position <=0.05 m, yaw <=0.05 rad, stopped linear <=0.01 m/s, angular <=0.02 rad/s, five logical ticks. The study checks arrival tick plus the preceding four raw samples; `arrivalGoalErrorMaxM` is the max of the exact arrival-tick errors, while `arrivalWindowPositionErrorMaxM` covers those five-sample windows. No tolerance was widened. Full development windows are retained in `evidence-B08/development-arrival-windows.json`.
